{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1793009479,"nonce":"NTU7iq3GSP7Ac/jwKRJXoN2P4VI=","title":"Enforce Cloud Sync expiry, retained storage and cloud-copy deletion","message":"Parent plan: e003324b4983bd187aa32106d22f198e4ad218eebe4eea5edb10793ef31e4b1a\n\nDefault expiresAt is server time plus 24 hours on first durable publication; retries, visits, compute restarts and ordinary incremental sync do not silently extend it. Allow explicit shorter/entitled longer durations, renewal, and a paid retained policy separate from login and compute-idle clocks. Check expiry synchronously at admission/read/write. Fence expired work, stop compute/PTY/extensions/previews and revoke access; schedule idempotent physical cleanup of R2 blobs/Git/checkpoints/exports/staging and provider disks/snapshots. Use the DO's single durable deadline scheduler plus reconciliation after exhausted retries; lifecycle rules only backstop abandoned data. Version renewal/deletion jobs so old cleanup cannot delete renewed data. Track physical cleanup before releasing byte accounting, retain bounded tombstones, cascade account deletion, and preserve all local files. Test duplicate/delayed alarms, outages, renewal races, partial cleanup and expired active clients.","files":null}]}